  "expectedText": "WEEK 39, 2026\n24 September 2026\n\nThis is a weekly newsletter that lists newly announced training programs addressing existential risk from AI. Visit AISafety.com/training for the full directory of upcoming programs.\n\n== NEW TRAINING PROGRAMS ==\n\n* Lens Academy: Deep Learning Theory\n  5–11 October · Online · Course\n  1 week · Full-time · No stipend · Entry bar: mid\n  Apply by 29 September\n  A new description & more <b>.\n  https://lensacademy.org/courses/theory-of-deep-learning?utm_source=aisafety.com&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=events-training-newsletter\n\n* AI Safety Camp (AISC): 12th edition\n  9 January – 26 April 2027 · Online · Fellowship\n  3 months · Part-time · No stipend · Entry bar: low\n  Applications to lead a project close 18 October\n  Small teams work on concrete AI safety projects, each guided by a project lead who brings the idea and plan. Approaches include technical, governance, advocacy, and theoretical foundations work. General applications open 7 November.\n  https://www.aisafety.camp/?utm_source=aisafety.com&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=events-training-newsletter\n\n* Mercial Research Fellowship: Autumn 2026\n  1 October – 1 November · Online · Fellowship\n  1 month · Part-time · No stipend · Entry bar: mid\n  Apply by 25 September\n  Mentored research program by the Mercial AI Safety Initiative. Streams cover why AI companies call for a slowdown, probe robustness, how long open-weight models will stay open, and whether to prioritize alignment research.\n  https://mercial.uk/fellowship?utm_source=aisafety.com&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=events-training-newsletter\n\n* Rethink Wellbeing: CBT Lab\n  week of 16 November · Online · Course\n  8 weeks · Part-time\n  Apply by 5 October for priority, 25 October at the latest\n  Mental health and productivity program. Groups of 4–6 people meet weekly with a facilitator to practice evidence-based tools for low energy, anxiety, imposter syndrome, and perfectionism. Free for people who have, or are working toward, a high positive impact through their career or donations – including in AI safety.\n  https://www.rethinkwellbeing.org/services?utm_source=aisafety.com&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=events-training-newsletter\n\nFull directory: https://aisafety.com/training?utm_source=training-newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=training-2026-week-39\n\nUnsubscribe: %UNSUBSCRIBELINK%\nView in browser: %WEBCOPY%\n%SENDER-INFO-SINGLELINE%\n"
